      "observed": "Q1 (IRLML6402 P-MOSFET) gate is tied to GND through R5 (47k) directly, and both throws of the SPDT switch SW1 are also connected to GND (common pin 2 to the gate node, pins 1 and 3 each to a GND symbol). There is no pull-up resistor from the gate to the source (BAT) net.",
      "expected": "The spec states SW1 is the optional power switch and that 'closing it pulls Q1's gate (through R5, 47k) low enough to turn the P-FET on and connect the battery; leaving it open keeps Q1 off and the battery disconnected.' For a high-side P-FET this requires the gate to be pulled up to the source (BAT) when the switch is open (e.g. R5 as a gate-to-source pull-up, with SW1 connecting the gate to GND only in the ON position).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "SW1, an SPDT switch, is the optional power switch: closing it pulls Q1's gate (through R5, 47k) low enough to turn the P-FET on and connect the battery; leaving it open keeps Q1 off and the battery disconnected."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet m5-pantilt (page 1), region C: R5 47k drawn vertically from the Q1 gate node down to a GND symbol; SW_SPDT SW1 with pin 2 to the same gate node and both pin 1 and pin 3 routed to GND."}
      ],
      "impact": "Vgs is held negative permanently, so Q1 is always ON: the battery at J5 is continuously connected to the /BAT bus pin and the optional power switch cannot disconnect it. The '(Optional) Power switch' feature is non-functional and the board can never be fully powered off from the battery.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the schematic matches the specification (values, part types, PWM/serial jumper topology, diode orientations, MAX3485 UART/A-B wiring). The one deviation I can read off the drawing is in the battery high-side switch: Q1's gate is pulled to GND by R5 and both SPDT throws of SW1 also go to GND with no gate-to-source pull-up, which contradicts the spec's 'open switch keeps Q1 off' and makes the optional power switch unable to disconnect the battery."
}

